// A world-placed destructible prop (barrel/crate/breakable wall) that the player can shoot. Unlike
// every other damageable non-enemy in this codebase (Mini Bomb/Decoy/Sentry, which f.Destroy the
// instant Health reaches 0), a Breakable is NOT destroyed on death - it persists so its View can
// show a distinct "broken" state. Breaking is driven from DamageUtility.ApplyDamage's non-Enemy
// death branch via BreakableUtility.TryBreak (a bolt-on TryGetPointer check, same shape as
// ExplodeOnDestroy) which flips Broken, disables the PhysicsCollider3D (collider->Enabled = false,
// the same idiom EnemySystem.OnEnemyDied uses) so the husk is walk-through and can't be hit again,
// and fires the BreakableBroken event the View reacts to.
//
// Deliberately state-ONLY: what (if anything) it drops on break is a separate, optional SpawnOnBreak
// component (see SpawnOnBreak.qtn) - a breakable WALL is just Breakable + Health + a collider and
// spawns nothing, while a loot barrel adds SpawnOnBreak. Health itself is likewise a separate
// authored component on the prototype (CurrentHealth == MaxHealth; 1 for a one-shot prop, higher for
// multi-hit) - it's what makes the prop shootable and triggers the break at 0.
//
// The collider must sit on a NON-"Enemy" physics layer: auto-aim (AimSystem) overlaps only the
// "Enemy" layer, so a Breakable is never an auto-target - it's only ever hit when a projectile
// physically passes through it or an explosion overlaps it, keeping aim-assist unambiguous.
component Breakable
{
    Boolean Broken;

    // Seconds a player must CONTINUOUSLY auto-target this before it breaks - a deliberate "hold the
    // reticle on the barrel for a moment" dwell rather than an instant pop the frame a shot lands.
    // Driven by BreakableFocusSystem while this is a weapon-holder's Aim.Target (which only happens
    // within AimSystem.BreakableTargetRange with no enemy competing). 0 disables the focus-break
    // entirely: such a prop breaks ONLY via damage (Health -> 0, the DamageUtility path) - e.g. a
    // breakable wall you shoot down. A prop can use either path or both (whichever triggers first).
    FP BreakDelay;

    // Accumulates DeltaTime while continuously auto-targeted; reset the moment targeting lapses (a
    // tick nobody aims at it). Reaches BreakDelay -> break. See BreakableFocusSystem.
    FP FocusTimer;

    // Tick this was last auto-targeted. Detects a lapse in targeting (so FocusTimer restarts from 0
    // rather than resuming) and dedups several players aiming at it in the same tick. See
    // BreakableFocusSystem.
    Int32 LastTargetedFrame;
}
